DOCUMENT();
loadMacros(
"PGstandard.pl",
"MathObjects.pl",
"PGML.pl"
);
Context("Numeric");
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstantFunctions=>0);
Context()->flags->set(reduceConstants=>0);

$fun_2 = Formula("cos((e^(x)))");
$fun_1 = Formula("((cos((5/(x)))))^(1/4)");

Context("Interval");

$set_ans_4 = Compute("{-7, 2, 4, 7} U ({-7, 2, 4, 7} U ({-9, -8, -2, 4, 5, 10})) U {-7, 2, 4, 7}");
$set_ans_5 = Compute("{-7, 2, 4, 7} U ({-7, 2, 4, 7}) U {-7, 2, 4, 7} U ({-9, -8, -2, 4, 5, 10}) U {-7, -5, 0, 9}");
$set_ans_6 = Compute("({-7, 2, 4, 7} - {-7, 2, 4, 7})");
$set_ans_1 = Compute("((1, 7)) - ((-infinity, infinity) - (({-1, 2, 10} U (({-1, 2, 10}))) U {-1, 2, 10})) U (1, 7)");
$set_ans_2 = Compute("{-1, 2, 10} U {-1, 2, 10} U {-1, 2, 10} - ((-infinity, infinity) - (1, 7))");
$set_ans_3 = Compute("(1, 7) U {-1, 2, 10} U (1, 7)");

Context("Vector");

BEGIN_PGML
# Questions:

_For arithmetic problems, if the result is not an integer, then retain *three significant digits*._

[`7*10+5`] is equal to [_____]{answer=>Real(75.),width=>6}
---

[`1+4-16-16.86*13`] is equal to [_____]{Real(-230.18)}
---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-1, 2, 10\}`]
- [`B = \{x | 1 < x < 7\}`]

Compute:
- [`(B) \cap ((A \cup ((A))) \cup A) \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_1}
- [`A \cup A \cup A \cap B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_2}
- [`B \cup A \cup B = `] [_____]{$set_ans_3}

---

Given the sets:
- [`A = \{-7, -5, 0, 9\}`]
- [`B = \{-9, -8, -2, 4, 5, 10\}`]
- [`C = \{-7, 2, 4, 7\}`]

Compute:
- [`C \cup (C \cup (B)) \cup C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_4}
- [`C \cup (C) \cup C \cup (B) \cup A = `] [_____]{$set_ans_5}
- [`C - C = `] [_____]{$set_ans_6}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 9, -8, -2 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -2, 4, 8 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle -8, 5, 3 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<9, -8, -2>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- [` \vec{u} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<9, -8, -2>") . Compute("<-8, 5, 3>")}
- [` \vec{v} \cdot \vec{w} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-2, 4, 8>") . Compute("<-8, 5, 3>")}
- [` \left\| \vec{w} \right\| = `] [_____]{norm(Compute("<-8, 5, 3>"))}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<9, -8, -2>"))}
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{v} `]. [_____]{Compute("<-2, 4, 8>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}

---

Suppose the vectors:
- [` \vec{u} = \langle 4, 4, -3 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{v} = \langle -7, 4, 10 \rangle `]
- [` \vec{w} = \langle 7, -7, 0 \rangle `]

Compute:
- Enter a vector in the same direction as [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{Compute("<7, -7, 0>")->cmp(parallel=>1,sameDirection=>1)}
- [` \vec{w} \cdot \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<7, -7, 0>") . Compute("<4, 4, -3>")}
- [` \vec{v} \times \vec{u} = `] [_____]{Compute("<-7, 4, 10>") x Compute("<4, 4, -3>")}
- Enter a vector parallel to [` \vec{u} `]. [_____]{Compute("<4, 4, -3>")->cmp(parallel=>1)}
- Enter a unit vector in the direction of [` \vec{w} `]. [_____]{unit(Compute("<7, -7, 0>"))}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_1]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->D()}
- [`f'(2) =`] [_____]{$fun_1->D()->eval(x=>2)}

---

Given this function:

>> [`[$fun_2]`] <<

Compute:
- [`f'(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()}
- [`f''(x) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->D()}
- [`f'(3) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>3)}
- [`f'(6) =`] [_____]{$fun_2->D()->eval(x=>6)}

---
END_PGML
ENDDOCUMENT();
